# Feature Reopen

<!-- prism:feature-reopen-contract:v1 -->

Reopen one `done` feature through exactly one route:

| Action | Source | Destination | Revalidation domains |
|---|---|---|---|
| `reopen-spec` | `done` + `none` | `specified` + `po` | specification, design, implementation, tests, release |
| `reopen-design` | `done` + `none` | `in-design` + `designer` | design, implementation, tests, release |
| `reopen-dev` | `done` + `none` | `in-dev` + `dev` | implementation, tests, release |

## Usage

`$feature-reopen [F-XXX] [specified|in-design|in-dev]`

The route selects the exact action. Do not accept a generic status setter or a
source other than `done` + `none`.

## Read-only review and confirmation

Resolve exactly one feature path and read SCHEMA, index, the complete feature,
linked design, requirements, API, delivery evidence, and workspace identity.
Use the optional probe with the matching action, for example:

```text
prism wiki transition-preflight F-XXX [path] --action reopen-dev --json
```

Require envelope schema 1, command facts, capability version 2 with a matching
action-specific surface, transition version 1, exact target owner, and a
consistent snapshot. A version string alone is insufficient; fall back to direct
file checks when needed. The preflight is copy-only and never authorizes a write.

A ready Copy request may initiate the impact review; no review record needs to
exist in the wiki before this action is requestable. The request remains
copy-only until the review and final confirmation are complete. Before proposing
a write, obtain a human-confirmed impact review that records:

- why the shipped feature needs reopening;
- the selected route and affected platforms;
- affected artifacts and any additional revalidation domains;
- the prior completion/release evidence that will be archived.

Show the full proposed write set, including the active `revalidation` list and
append-only reopen-history record. The existing delivery evidence cannot silently
satisfy a new Done check: archive the current evidence in the history record,
remove it from the active Delivery evidence section on confirmation, and require
unaffected evidence to be explicitly reaffirmed after review. Show exact affected
platform-requirement and API pages with their proposed invalidated statuses;
preserve prior statuses in the history and never reset unrelated shared contracts.

Reread the feature, index, identity, and linked context immediately before asking
for confirmation and once after confirmation. On confirmation, update the feature
route, set the pending revalidation domains, archive the prior delivery evidence,
update the index, and append the log. Preserve prior history. Decline or cancel
means no mutation. If a multi-file write is partial, report exact changes and stop
for fresh recovery; no transaction is implied.

Return the prior route, new route, impact review, affected artifacts, active
revalidation domains, and archived evidence. Reopening does not claim that the
feature is again ready, implemented, tested, or shipped.
